old and moist.", "locator": "Book II, Chap. 192 'Of Chickweed', The Temperature", "not_counted_why": "'As Galen saith' sits inside the sentence, so under your rule this is a report rather than Gerard's own reading. Shown, not counted.", "note": "'As Galen saith' sits inside the sentence, so under your rule this is a report rather than Gerard's own reading. Shown, not counted.", "short": "Gerard (1633)", "source": "John Gerard, The Herball or Generall Historie of Plantes, enlarged by Thomas Johnson (1633 text; read in the Ex-Classics transcription and checked against the 1636 printing scanned at archive.org)", "tier": "second-hand-report", "tradition": "Galenic (European)", "url": "https://www.exclassics.com/herbal/herball.txt", "year": "1633"}, {"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (cool); agrees with the app moisture (moist).", "assigns_moisture": "Moist", "assigns_temperature": "Cold", "corpus": "galenic-european", "counted": true, "counted_moisture": true, "counted_temperature": true, "excerpt": "Alsine. Chickweed. Is cold and moist without any binding, assuages swelling, and comforts the sinews much", "gloss": "Chickweed is cold and moist without any binding.", "locator": "Catalogue of simples, Herbs, 'Alsine' (Gutenberg #49513, offset ~842102)", "not_counted_why": "", "note": "Culpeper's entry ends with the reference '_Galen._' after the sentence, in the way he cites an authority at the end of an entry, not inside the reading. Counted as his own.", "short": "Culpeper (1653)", "source": "Nicholas Culpeper, The Complete Herbal (text of 1653; London: Thomas Kelly, 1850 edition as digitised by Project Gutenberg #49513)", "tier": "first-hand", "tradition": "Galenic (European)", "url": "https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/49513/pg49513.txt", "year": "1653"}, {"agreement": "Counted: agrees with the app temperature (cool); agrees with the app moisture (moist).", "assigns_moisture": "Moist", "assigns_temperature": "Cold", "corpus": "galenic-european",